WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.580
Environmental risk assessment combines forecast information, a site survey, aircraft limits,

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.432
crew capability, mission complexity, and current observations.

00:00:07.432 --> 00:00:12.319
It should produce explicit go or no-go criteria rather than a vague

00:00:12.319 --> 00:00:14.356
sense that conditions look acceptable.

00:00:14.356 --> 00:00:19.244
Check weather from appropriate current sources, then compare it with the site.

00:00:19.244 --> 00:00:23.317
Observe wind indicators, gusts, visibility, precipitation, cloud, temperature, sun angle,

00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:25.353
terrain effects, and changing activity.

00:00:25.353 --> 00:00:27.797
Record material differences from the forecast.

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:31.463
Survey launch, recovery, route, obstacles, people, vehicles, radio conditions,

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.092
and emergency landing options.

00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:36.351
Identify hazards, consequence, likelihood, controls, and residual risk.

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:39.202
Assign an owner for each important control.

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:43.682
Brief the crew on the objective, limits, battery thresholds, communication terms,

00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:48.570
loss-of-link behavior, weather triggers, emergency areas, and who can call a stop.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.421
Shared expectations reduce delay when conditions change.

00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:53.050
Monitor trends during flight.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.901
Wind, visibility, battery performance, signal quality, lighting,

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.345
and ground activity can deteriorate gradually.

00:00:58.345 --> 00:01:04.048
Use early thresholds that preserve time and energy for a controlled return and landing.

00:01:04.048 --> 00:01:06.084
Document the decision and outcome.

00:01:06.084 --> 00:01:10.157
A canceled flight can be evidence of good risk management.

00:01:10.157 --> 00:01:14.230
After the mission, compare expected and actual conditions, capture lessons,

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:20.340
and adjust future margins without turning one successful flight into permission for less conservative behavior.
